{
  "name": "oil-beetle",
  "_about": "The black oil beetle (Meloe proscarabaeus), a female 3 cm long: a huge soft swollen abdomen, its segments ringed, blue-black and dull, with two short wing cases overlapping over its front only and gaping apart behind (it cannot fly); a big head on a narrow pronotum; beaded antennae; long legs. It oozes an oily, blistering fluid from its knees when touched. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
